// A `validated` service operation, emitted through a requirement. The frontend
// admits it. The wasm reference REFUSES it by name (issue #1373): a validated
// crossing needs the response-validation seam and this tier has none. The same
// document without `validated` emits, so the modifier is the only reason for
// the refusal.
//
// It is a service operation and not an extern on purpose: the self-host gate
// (selfhost/lower.rvl) does not parse `validated` on an extern yet, so an extern
// carrier here would be a false-reject in tools/gate_reference_census.py.
//
// This is not a byte-agreement case, so it cannot live in the tier's CORPUS.
// The line-coverage gate drives the reference over it here, which is the only
// way the RevlError-to-EmitError translation in
//
//   backends/wasm/emit.py::_refuse_validated_emissions
//
// ever runs (issue #1431). The same wrapper's ModuleNotFoundError bootstrap is
// NOT reached by this or any document: it runs only when emit.py is executed
// as a script with revl not importable. The refusal's text is asserted by
// tests/test_validated_tier_refusal_1373.py.
//
// selfhost/emit_wasm.rvl has no counterpart to this refusal: it does not
// read the `validated` modifier.
service Model { emission validated fn complete(h: Str) -> Str }
component Agent requires model: Model {
  emit model.complete("p")
}
